For exothermic reaction $\begin{aligned}
\Delta \mathrm{H}=& \mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{P}}-\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{R}} < 0 \\
& \mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{B}}-\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{A}} < 0 \\
& \mathbf{E}_{\mathrm{B}} < \mathbf{E}_{\mathrm{A}}
\end{aligned}$
Catalyst does not changes the initial and final position of the reaction so correct answer is (A)

$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{K}=\frac{\mathrm{A}_{0}-\mathrm{A}_{\mathrm{t}}}{\mathrm{t}} \\
\mathrm{K}=\frac{\mathrm{A}_{2}}{2 \mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}} \\
\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=\frac{\mathrm{A}_{0}}{2 \mathrm{ K}} \quad \text{ Zero order }
\end{array}\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2} \propto$ initial concentration so double times
